      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T12:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Awaitility\u0027s untilAsserted only retries on AssertionError - any other throwable, including the checked ExecutionException and InterruptedException from future.get(), is rethrown as-is through a sneaky-throw, so these signatures now understate what callers can receive and a caller can no longer write catch (ExecutionException e) around them. Could the poll body convert a read failure into an AssertionError so it is retried, and the throws clauses be kept where an exception really can escape?",
      "revId": "febc9de080c2ade0848082c16fc7322ef7b57cd0",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "995d6aa2_7d9e63e0",
        "filename": "testtool-util/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/protocol/util/CheckUtil.java",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 9229
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T11:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Handled in the poll body: a failed read now becomes an AssertionError so it gets retried with the cause preserved, and an interrupt restores the interrupt flag and aborts the poll with an unchecked exception.",
      "parentUuid": "9fa629bf_8c6e764e",
      "revId": "febc9de080c2ade0848082c16fc7322ef7b57cd0",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f55e5920_420e0818",
        "filename": "testtool-util/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/protocol/util/CheckUtil.java",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T12:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This needs careful consideration. Awaitility defaults catchUncaughtExceptions to true - so for as long as any of these helpers is polling it installs a JVM-global default uncaught-exception handler and rethrows anything that lands there — a dying background thread now fails whichever check happens to be waiting, with that thread\u0027s exception. The old Stopwatch loops did not do this. Please consult the documentation of Awaitility.defaultCatchUncaughtExceptions behaviour and its impact here.",
      "revId": "febc9de080c2ade0848082c16fc7322ef7b57cd0",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
